{"id": "section-body-06306", "title": "Management of Epilepsy", "chapterId": "chapter-eight", "blocks": [{"id": "body-06306", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Management of Epilepsy", "runs": [{"text": "Management"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Epilepsy"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1659"}}, {"id": "body-06307", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Epilepsy is a common neurological disorder characterised by recurring seizures. About two-thirds of people with active epilepsy have their epilepsy controlled satisfactorily with anti-seizure medication (ASM). Other treatment approaches may include surgery and neuromodulation. Optimal management is required to improve patient’s health outcomes and minimise detrimental impacts on social, educational, and occupational activities.", "runs": [{"text": "Epilepsy is a common neurological disorder characterised by recurring seizures. About two-thirds of people with active epilepsy have their epilepsy controlled satisfactorily with anti-seizure medication (ASM). Other treatment approaches may include surgery and neuromodulation. Optimal management is required to improve patient’s health outcomes and minimise detrimental impacts on social, educational, and occupational activities."}]}, {"id": "body-06309", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-06310", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Recurrent seizures", "runs": [{"text": "Recurrent"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "seizures"}]}, {"id": "body-06313", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Investigations", "runs": [{"text": "Investigations"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-06314", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Serum electrolytes, random blood glucose", "runs": [{"text": "Serum"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "electrolytes,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "random"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "blood"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "glucose"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1642"}}, {"id": "body-06315", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Serum antiseizure medication levels", "runs": [{"text": "Serum"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "antiseizure"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "medication"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "levels"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1642"}}, {"id": "body-06316", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Electroencephalogram (EEG)", "runs": [{"text": "Electroencephalogram"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(EEG)"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1642"}}, {"id": "body-06318", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Brain CT scan", "runs": [{"text": "Brain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "CT"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "scan"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1642"}}, {"id": "body-06319", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Brain MRI with epilepsy protocol", "runs": [{"text": "Brain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "MRI"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "epilepsy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "protocol"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1642"}}, {"id": "body-06322", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Classification of epileptic syndromes", "runs": [{"text": "Classification"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "epileptic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "syndromes"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-06323", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Classify epileptic seizures and epilepsy syndromes in all patients using a multi-axial diagnostic scheme (refer to ILAE classification) as failure to classify the epilepsy syndrome correctly can lead to inappropriate treatment and persistence of seizures.", "runs": [{"text": "Classify epileptic seizures and epilepsy syndromes in all patients using a multi-axial diagnostic scheme (refer to ILAE classification) as failure to classify the epilepsy syndrome correctly can lead to inappropriate treatment and persistence of "}, {"text": "seizures."}]}, {"id": "body-06325", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-06326", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Utilize a single ASM (monotherapy) and increase dose until seizures are controlled or side effects cannot be tolerated.", "runs": [{"text": "Utilize"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "single ASM"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(monotherapy)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "increase"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "until"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "seizures"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "controlled"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "side"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "effects"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cannot"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be "}, {"text": "tolerated."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1642"}}, {"id": "body-06327", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "If the initial treatment is unsuccessful, initiate alternative monotherapy with different medication before resorting to drug combinations.", "runs": [{"text": "If"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "initial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "treatment"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "unsuccessful,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "initiate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "alternative"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "monotherapy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "different"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "medication"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "before"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "resorting"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to drug combinations."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1642"}}, {"id": "body-06328", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Combination therapy (adjunctive or 'add-on' therapy) should only be considered when attempts at monotherapy with ASM s have not resulted in seizure freedom.", "runs": [{"text": "Combination therapy (adjunctive or 'add-on' therapy) should only be considered when attempts at monotherapy with ASM s have not resulted in seizure freedom."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1642"}}, {"id": "body-06329", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "If trials of combination therapy do not bring about worthwhile benefits, revert treatment to the initial monotherapy regimen that has proved most acceptable to the patient and consider referral for expert evaluation.", "runs": [{"text": "If trials of combination therapy do not bring about worthwhile benefits, revert treatment to the initial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "monotherapy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "regimen"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "has"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "proved"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "most"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "acceptable"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "consider"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "referral for expert evaluation."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1642"}}, {"id": "body-06331", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "For management of status epilepticus—refer to emergency and critical care chapter 1", "runs": [{"text": "For"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "management"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "status"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "epilepticus—refer"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "emergency"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "critical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "care"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chapter"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "1"}]}, {"id": "body-06333", "type": "heading", "style": "Headin